\title{Generalized element}
\taxon{Definition}
\author{hsuchingchung}
\date{2026-10-30T13:20:46Z}
\import{macros-subobj}

\p{Let #{A} be an object in a category \CCat. A \strong{generalize element} of #{A} is a morphism into #{A} 

##{x : \Gamma \r A.}

The source #{\Gamma} of #{x} is called the \strong{context} of #{x}. In the case \CCat has terminal object #{1}, a generalized element #{x : 1 \rightarrow A} of #{A} whose context is the terminal object #{1} is called a \strong{global element} of #{A}.}